assigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Right heart failure, pulmonary embolism and deep venous thrombosis"},{"label":"B","text":"Elephantiasis, deep venous thrombosis, Kaposi sarcoma"},{"label":"C","text":"Liver failure, heart failure, chronic renal failure"},{"label":"D","text":"Elephantiasis, cellulitis and pulmonary embolism"},{"label":"E","text":"Cellulitis, deep venous thrombosis, pulmonary oedema"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-dc0f1a22e9e3","stem":"Regarding Hookworm infestation","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Parasitology","topic":"Medical Parasitology","topicOriginal":"Medical Parasitology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is usually spread by the faeco-oral route"},{"label":"B","text":"May block the pancreatic duct causing pancreatitis"},{"label":"C","text":"In early stage may present with a dry cough and asthmatic wheezing."},{"label":"D","text":"Eggs can be readily distinguished microscopically from those of Strongyloides sp."},{"label":"E","text":"It is diagnosed by microscopy of adhesive tape prints taken from the perianal area"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Parasitology","displayTopic":"Medical Parasitology","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e1b0329cf658","stem":"Following an occupation needle stick injury with HIV- infected blood","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"Hiv","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Zidovudine and Lamivudine for 28 days reduce the chance of sero- conversion for about 8%"},{"label":"B","text":"Zidovudine and Lamivudine should be started 24 hours post exposure"},{"label":"C","text":"Infection is more likely if the HIV patient is in the window period"},{"label":"D","text":"Monotherapy treatment is as effective as two drugs therapy"},{"label":"E","text":"The risk of HIV transmission is about 30%"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0fd3930663ba","stem":"A thirty five year old man presents in a clinic with history of chronic productive cough that is worse in the morning and brought on by changes in posture. Sputum is copious and yellow. The most likely diagnosis is","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"ENT","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Bronchiectasis"},{"label":"B","text":"Bronchial asthma"},{"label":"C","text":"Chronic bronchitis"},{"label":"D","text":"Pulmonary tuberculosis"},{"label":"E","text":"Bronchogenic carcinoma MULTIPLE TRUE/FALSE QUESTIONS"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"ENT","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-53eacc668a83","stem":"Regarding the management of a patient admitted in a medical ward with diagnosis of infective endocarditis","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"FALSE Liver function test is used to monitor progress"},{"label":"B","text":"TRUE Treat Dental problem if present"},{"label":"C","text":"TRUE Success relies on eradication of pathogen 11"},{"label":"D","text":"FALSE Bacteriostatic regiment should be used"},{"label":"E","text":"TRUE Surgery is used mainly to cope with structural complications"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"d3e903480f49adc43e487e998f5ffb471acbbdbb"},{"id":"q-50d3b22fbe02","stem":"Regarding presentation of patient with Peptic Ulcer diseased","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","topicOriginal":"Gastroenterology and Hepatology","subtopic":"Peptic","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"TRUE Pain-meal relation can be used to differentiate between duodenal and gastric ulcer"},{"label":"B","text":"TRUE Sudden onset of severe, generalized abdominal pain may indicate perforation"},{"label":"C","text":"TRUE Food relieve the pain of duodenal ulcers and minimal relief for gastric ulcer"},{"label":"D","text":"FALSE Dyspepsia that radiate to the back indicate bleeding peptic ulcer diseases"},{"label":"E","text":"FALSE Pain worsening 2-3 hours after meals suggest gastric ulcer"}],"priority":1,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":f