 both ketogenic and glucogenic."},{"label":"B","text":"Both sulphur containing amino acids are essential amino acids."},{"label":"C","text":"Aminotransferase enzymes require pyridoxal phosphate as a co-enzyme."},{"label":"D","text":"The average man has a store of about 1kg of free amino acids."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Water, pH and Buffers","answerAuditStatus":"independently_reasoned_provisional_oct20","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5bc4f1ed182f","stem":"Which metabolic abnormality gives rise to the serious disease phenylketonuria?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Metabolism · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Metabolism","options":[{"label":"A","text":"Homocysteine cannot be converted into methionine"},{"label":"B","text":"Phenylalanine cannot be converted into tyrosine"},{"label":"C","text":"Phenylalanine cannot be converted into alanine"},{"label":"D","text":"Tyrosine cannot be converted into phenylalanine"}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Metabolism · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"independent_no_source_key_bulk_v4","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-1ecb2d4aacc5","stem":"Which of the following statements about the deamination of amino acids is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Medical Biochemistry","topic":"Water, pH and Buffers","topicOriginal":"Water, pH and Buffers","subtopic":"Acid","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Most amino acids are directly deaminated by dehydrogenation reactions."},{"label":"B","text":"Most amino acids are deaminated by a two-step transdeamination process."},{"label":"C","text":"Most amino acids are deaminated by transferring their amino groups to oxaloacetate."},{"label":"D","text":"Most amino acids are deaminated by irreversible transamination reactions."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Medical Biochemistry","displayTopic":"Water, pH and Buffers","answerAuditStatus":"reasoned_without_reference","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"provisional_answer","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[],"manualEdits":{}},{"id":"q-6f2033f090fe","stem":"Which of the following statements about the mechanism of transamination reactions is correct?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"ATP hydrolysis is used to transfer the amino group on the Schiff base to the carbonyl group of keto acid acceptor."},{"label":"B","text":"The first step of a transamination reaction is the formation of a Schiff base between pyridoxal-5'-phosphate and the carbonyl group of the keto acid."},{"label":"C","text":"The first step of a transamination reaction is the formation of a Schiff base between the carbonyl group of pyridoxal-5'-phosphate and the amino group of the amino acid. 20"},{"label":"D","text":"The first step of a transamination reaction is the formation of a Schiff base between pyridoxamine phosphate and the keto acid."}],"priority":2,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["subject_unclassified","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFla