ext":"the apneustic center of the pons Question 21 What is the primary regulator of the magnitude of alveolar"},{"label":"A","text":"the H+ concentration in the brain extracellular fluid, which is monitored by central chemoreceptors"},{"label":"B","text":"The PO2 of the arterial blood, which is monitored by central chemoreceptors"},{"label":"C","text":"The PO2 of the arterial blood, which is monitored by peripheral chemoreceptors"},{"label":"D","text":"stretch receptors in the lung Question 22 Which correctly describes the cause of the increase in alveolar ventilation that occurs when a person ascends to"},{"label":"A","text":"The decrease in PCO2 of inspired air decreases alveolar PCO2, stimulating the peripheral chemoreceptors."},{"label":"B","text":"The decrease in PCO2 of inspired air decreases alveolar PCO2, stimulating the central chemoreceptors."},{"label":"C","text":"The decrease in PO2 of inspired air decreases alveolar and arterial PO2, stimulating the peripheral chemoreceptors."},{"label":"D","text":"The decrease in total atmospheric pressure causes a greater negative pressure in the intrapleural space, resulting in deeper and more frequent breathing. Question"}],"priority":2,"status":"review","flags":["too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Human Anatomy","displayTopic":"Neuroanatomy","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization","whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-9816be877846","stem":"Which one of the following substances is LEAST","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Unclassified Health Sciences","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":n